        <h1>Privacy Policy for Money Left</h1>
        <div class="effective-date"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> September 26, 2026</div>
        
        <p>TP Digital ("we", "our", or "us") operates the Money Left mobile application (the "App"). This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your information when you use our application.</p>
        
        <h2>Our Commitment to Privacy</h2>
        <p>Money Left is designed with a <strong>local-first architecture</strong>. All your financial logs, expense amounts, custom categories, remarks, savings goals, and historical records are stored strictly on your device using a secure local database.</p>
        
        <h2>Information Collection and Use</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Local Data Storage:</strong> All data generated while using Money Left remains entirely on your device. We do not collect, transmit, upload, or store your personal financial data, income records, or spending analytics on any external servers.</li>
            <li><strong>No Personal Data Harvesting:</strong> We do not require account registration, login credentials, or personal identifiers (such as name, email address, or phone number) to use the core features of the App.</li>
            <li><strong>Diagnostics and Updates:</strong> If you download updates via the Google Play Store, Google LLC may collect standard anonymous diagnostic data and crash logs in accordance with the Google Play Store Terms of Service.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>The App may utilize standard platform services (such as Google Play services for app distribution and in-app updates) which operate under their own respective privacy policies. We do not share any user data with third-party advertisers or analytics networks.</p>
        
        <h2>Data Security & Backups</h2>
        <p>Because your data is stored locally on your device, you maintain total ownership and control. If you use the optional offline backup feature, your exported data bundle (.mlbak) is stored directly by you. You can clear or delete all recorded history at any time by clearing app data or uninstalling the application.</p>
        
        <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted within this section with an updated effective date.</p>
        
        <h2>Contact Us</h2>
        <p>If you have any questions or suggestions about this Privacy Policy, please reach out via our developer profile or support channels under TP Digital.</p>
